  4→ * The ONLY effect surface of the agent path: every consequential or
  5→ * read-only action the agent takes goes through `SolutionToolPort.call`
  6→ * as a typed `SolutionToolCommand` carrying full attribution (the raw
  7→ * utterance, the EXACT normalized command — the typed intent serialized
  8→ * canonically — the compiler path, agent/user attribution). The agent
  9→ * NEVER generates geometry, NEVER writes raw state and NEVER claims
 10→ * validation success: the port's responses are ECHOED with their
 11→ * authority labels ("solution-engine" / "solution-graph" /
 12→ * "solution-boq-service"), never re-authored.
 13→ *
 14→ * The PRODUCTION binding — the deterministic solution engine (PROD-022)
 15→ * plus the BOQ derivation services (PROD-025) — is wired by the Tech Lead
 16→ * at composition time (PROD-024/026 era). This module ships:
 17→ *
 18→ *  - the `SolutionToolPort` interface and the typed command/response
 19→ *    model (validate, apply, inspect, navigate, explain, boq-step-lookup —
 20→ *    exactly the tool families the work order names);
 21→ *  - `toolCommandOf` — the canonical tool-command builder used by the
 22→ *    compiler (with each tool kind's normalized command text);
 23→ *  - `createInMemorySolutionToolDouble` — a clearly-labeled IN-MEMORY
 24→ *    TEST DOUBLE (not the production engine): deterministic, offline,
