  1→/**
  2→ * AISE-021 — browser engineering workspace: STRUCTURAL INPUT MODEL.
  3→ *
  4→ * ⚠⚠⚠ NO BROWSER-SIDE AUTHORITY (frozen invariant, spec/architecture-lock.md
  5→ * "Authority" #8: UI state is never canonical) ⚠⚠⚠
  6→ *
  7→ * Everything in this module is READ-ONLY DISPLAY DATA. The workspace NEVER
  8→ * fetches, NEVER computes engineering truth, NEVER alters review state and
  9→ * NEVER writes anything back. All facts arrive fully assembled by the server
 10→ * inside `WorkspaceInput` (a drawing pinned to a graph version + a graph
 11→ * snapshot slice + evidence records + an optional server-computed review
 12→ * state + the currently selected node id). The rendered HTML — including the
 13→ * review banner and the selection highlight — is a PROJECTION of that input,
 14→ * nothing more. Selecting a node changes ONLY presentation
 15→ * (`data-selected="true"` attributes + the selection panel), never data.
 16→ *
 17→ * BOUNDARY MATRIX (tools/lib/boundaries.ts): apps may import apps/packages
 18→ * ONLY — apps/web CANNOT import backend/api sources. Therefore the input
 19→ * types below are STRUCTURAL MIRRORS of the backend shapes (AISE-020
 20→ * `Drawing2D` family and the AISE-016 `GraphVersion` slice consumed by
 21→ * AISE-020's `ProjectionInput`): same field names, same JSON shapes, defined
 22→ * locally. A real backend `Drawing2D`/`GraphVersion` serialized over the wire
 23→ * satisfies these types as-is (structural typing); the AUTHORITATIVE
 24→ * generators stay in the backend (AISE-016/020). This module deliberately
 25→ * imports NOTHING.
 26→ */
 27→
 28→/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 29→/* 2D drawing structural mirror (AISE-020 projections/model.ts)        */
 30→/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 31→
 32→/** Immutable 2D point in drawing units (after the coordinate frame). */
 33→export type Point2D = readonly [number, number];
